From f04d7d5f4d5628927f5c09f93f345e4e07ffe470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Keller <christoph.keller@gmx.net>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:32:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cursor: mark fully transparent 32bpp pixels in the AND mask

For ARGB cursors xorgxrdp sends 32bpp pointer data with an all-zero AND
mask and relies on the client honouring the alpha channel. Clients that
ignore alpha (e.g. Jump Desktop) treat every pixel as opaque and draw the
transparent area around the pointer as a black box.

Set the AND mask bit for pixels whose alpha is 0. Their XOR value is 0
(premultiplied ARGB), so AND=1/XOR=0 is transparent for every client;
alpha-aware clients render exactly as before. Semi-transparent pixels
(e.g. shadows) are unchanged.

Reproduce/verify without such a client: dump the pointer PDUs a FreeRDP
client receives (LD_PRELOAD on freerdp_image_copy_from_pointer_data) and
count alpha==0 pixels not covered by the AND mask. Yaru cursor (GNOME,
32x32 pointer): 730 of 1024 pixels before, 0 after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VLJpmVyG6ghcutrcFH3F8v
---
 module/rdpCursor.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/module/rdpCursor.c b/module/rdpCursor.c
index e199653..784a7a0 100644
--- a/module/rdpCursor.c
+++ b/module/rdpCursor.c
@@ -325,6 +325,14 @@ rdpSpriteSetCursorCon(rdpClientCon *clientCon,
                     set_pixel_safe(cur_data, index,
                                    (sending_height - 1) - jndex,
                                    sending_width, sending_height, 32, pixel);
+                    /* fully transparent: mark in the AND mask too, for
+                     * clients that ignore the alpha channel */
+                    if ((pixel & 0xff000000) == 0)
+                    {
+                        set_pixel_safe(cur_mask, index,
+                                       (sending_height - 1) - jndex,
+                                       sending_width, sending_height, 1, 1);
+                    }
                 }
             }
         }
